ral, and add a test fixture asserting the tolerated wording variants map to exit 0.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["3 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the positive rationale for casting the final Verified vote via scripts/cast_gerrit_verified_vote.py: the pinned gerrit-review-action exposes no hook to classify Gerrit output, so a trusted repo helper is the only place to distinguish a benign closed-change race from a real fail-closed error while reusing the proven SSH/chmod-600/known_hosts pattern already in the triage-comment step.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.6114,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["The plan says to 'Replace only the final ... gerrit-review-action invocation with a trusted repo helper' and gives trust-boundary and message-shape reasons, but no stated rationale for the helper-vs-lighter-alternative structural decision (e.g. why not an inline conditional wrapping the existing SSH pattern).","ABSENCE: G6(4) requires a POSITIVE rationale for the chosen approach; the plan's rationale covers the checkout boundary but not the reimplementation-as-helper choice.","The reimplementation is well-grounded in existing patterns (gerrit-verify.yaml:574-618 comment step; voter.py:726-740 c943 closed-change precedent), so the approach is sound -- only the stated rationale is thin."],"finding":"The plan does not state a positive rationale for why the fix reimplements the full Gerrit SSH `gerrit review` cast in a new repo helper (scripts/cast_gerrit_verified_vote.py) rather than a lighter-touch alternative; it explains the default-branch trust boundary and the action's lack of a custom-message input, but not why a whole helper is the right structural choice for a closed-change-tolerance fix.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fc14cd886e8cc3cae","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan section 'Plan' / 'Result classification and safety guards'","norm_id":"nd5422400baa4055f","priority":0.1886,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An implementer or future reviewer questions why the fix grows a new script instead of tolerating the closed-change error inline within the existing action/step."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add one sentence to the Plan section noting the action is