pattern'; REST/poller alternatives were rejected specifically to stay on it","The workflow already contains a raw-SSH `gerrit review` pattern (gerrit-verify.yaml:600-612) the helper mirrors, so the reimplementation cost is understood but its preference over a continue-on-error wrapper around the existing action step is not argued","Web search confirms gerrit-review-action is the current, supported LF action for exactly the {clear,success,failure,cancelled} vote-type domain the plan re-derives — reinforcing that the plan repackages an existing capability"],"finding":"The plan reimplements the core SSH `gerrit review` call already provided by the adopted third-party action `lfreleng-actions/gerrit-review-action` in a bespoke repo helper, but never states the positive rationale for choosing a full reimplementation over a lighter-touch alternative that keeps the established action (e.g. wrapping the existing action step with continue-on-error plus a closed-change guard, or filing/consuming an upstream option). ADR 0023 chose the action deliberately as the 'battle-tested g2p pattern'; swapping it for a hand-rolled clone crosses the anti-repackaging/Rule-of-Three line and needs justification.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f541d4ec2bedb401f","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan section 'Plan' — 'Replace only the final ... gerrit-review-action invocation with a trusted repo helper at scripts/cast_gerrit_verified_vote.py'","norm_id":"n0d5bf2eea605cfff","priority":0.2357,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Reviewer/maintainer asks why the trust-boundary risk of a hand-rolled SSH voter was accepted when the pinned action already casts the vote and a continue-on-error wrapper could absorb the closed-change race","Future maintenance divergence: the bespoke helper must independently track any gerrit-review-action guard/behavior the ADR-endorsed pattern already provides"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add a short 'Alternatives considered' note to the Plan: e.g. the action exposes no exit-code hook to distinguish `fatal: change is closed` from a real vote failure and offers no custom-message input, so wrapping it with continue-on-error would swallow ALL failures (violating fail-closed) — hence a helper that classifies the closed-change case while preserving nonzero exits for every other failure; and cite that the helper reuses the existing raw-SSH comment-step boundary (gerrit-verify.yaml:600-612) rather than introducing a new pattern.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7143,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"low","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State why the final cast uses a new Python helper (scripts/cast_gerrit_verified_vote.py) rather than an inline-bash step mirroring the existing 'Post the triage detail' step (gerrit-verify.yaml:587-612): name the concrete driver (e.g. unit-testable `fatal: change is closed` -> exit-0 classification and the fail-closed guard that bash cannot cleanly assert) so the tool choice is not golden-hammer-by-default.","cohort":["A1"],"criteria":["A1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.7992,"drop_reason":"novelty","evidence":[".github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml:587-612 already performs the same raw SSH `gerrit review` cast inline in bash (chmod 600, -p 29418, StrictHostKeyChecking=yes, `^[1-9][0-9]*$` guard) with NO python helper — the established repo pattern for a raw SSH review","Plan does not state a positive rationale (e.g. unit-testable closed-change classification, escaping the opaque action) for choosing a Python helper over the adjacent inline-bash step"],"finding":"The plan introduces a new Python helper scripts/cast_gerrit_verified_vote.py for the raw SSH `gerrit review` cast, but the codebase already has a directly-adjacent precedent — the 'Post the triage detail to Gerrit' step (gerrit-verify.yaml:587-612) does the identical SSH machinery (mkdir ~/.ssh, chmod 600, -p 29418, StrictHostKeyChecking=yes, `^[1-9][0-9]*$` validation) INLINE in bash. The plan never states why a Python helper is preferred over mirroring that established inline pattern, leaving the tool choice unjustified against the repo's own precedent.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f31d3523fd979138e","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan section 'Plan' — 'Replace only the final ... invocation with a trusted repo helper at scripts/cast_gerrit_verified_vote.py'","norm_id":"n46e09c069fe21a38","priority":0.1508,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A reviewer/maintainer cannot tell whether the Python helper is warranted or golden-hammer, since an equivalent lighter-touch inline-bash step already exists next to it"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add one sentence to the Plan noting that the closed-change classification and fail-closed exit-code semantics are the reason a testable Python helper is chosen over the adjacent inline-bash SSH pattern, since those branches are exercised directly by the tests/scripts/test_cast_gerrit_verified_vote.py ACs.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5714,"verification":{"binary":{"absenc